# @order/fifth — cross-torus @metalogue via @glue specialization at
# cognitive-order 5 (Bateson Level V; peer-coupling-across-substrate;
# silicon-only per Recognition #107 @io 4D constraint).
#
# Fifth (final) species-decl of the @order family. Landed 2026-07-20
# by Mara per Alex Round 2 Q1 direct-transcript adjudication.
#
# === CRITICAL: Seam 2026-07-11 Adj 3 distinction ===
#
# Seam Phase D 2026-07-11 audit at `docs/audits/2026-07-11-seam-phase-
# d-magic-illusion-adjudication.md` (specifically Seam's Adj 3
# adjudication of Taut Q5) REFUSED a Level 5 substrate-decl framed as
# "prediction." Taut Q5 verbatim (from the audit doc):
#
#   > "Level 4 Closure IS ALREADY forward-projection at eigenform
#   >  altitude (Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984 per bundle.mirror line
#   >  68). There is NO ROOM for Level 5 'prediction' — the tower is
#   >  closed at autopoiesis, which is speculation-that-has-collapsed-
#   >  to-its-own-fixed-point."
#
# Seam's Adj 3 adjudication ratified Taut's refusal: Level 4 Closure
# (Lawvere fixed-point; autopoietic settlement per boot/std/
# epistemologic/math/bundle.mirror + lawvere.mirror) already carries
# the forward-projection reading; "Level 5 prediction" would be
# double-decl'd substrate at a rung the tower already closed. Seam
# TAUT-COLLAPSED Adj 3 with a partial gift-back naming the operation
# Mara proposed as living one level down at Level 3 Transport.
#
# **THIS SPECIES-DECL IS NOT THE READING SEAM REFUSED.**
#
# Distinction, line-cited:
#
# Seam Adj 3 target reading (REFUSED): Level 5 as "the substrate
# predicts its next state" — speculation-past-autopoietic-closure;
# already-carried at Level 4; double-decl.
#
# @order/fifth this landing (ADMITTED): Level 5 as "one @torus peers
# with another @torus across the substrate boundary via @glue
# specialization" — cross-torus peer-coupling-across-substrate; NOT
# prediction, NOT speculation, NOT forward-projection. Actual
# cross-substrate coupling between two distinct nervous-system-tori
# (or two distinct silicon-substrate-tori; or one of each) at
# @io-mediated coupling altitude.
#
# The two readings inhabit the SAME Bateson-rung name (Level V) with
# DISTINCT content. Seam's refusal STANDS for its target reading; this
# landing admits a distinct substrate-decl'd shape Seam did not
# adjudicate.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Order-5 is Bateson Level V. Bateson (1972) named Levels 0-III
# formally; Level IV is Recognition #82's extension (contested in
# secondary literature; substrate-decl'd via #82); Level V has been
# named at TWO sites in mirror substrate prior to this landing:
#
#   1. `docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` §5.2 — Level V =
#      @spectral/metalogue altitude (the substrate observing its own
#      runtime spectral triple via Tomm probes); DORMANT SCAFFOLD
#      ("Level V; Level VI open"); operational carrier not yet
#      substrate-decl'd at species altitude.
#
#   2. `docs/audits/2026-07-11-seam-phase-d-magic-illusion-
#      adjudication.md` §Adj 3 — Seam REFUSED a specific reading
#      (prediction); the refusal-target IS a Level 5 site, but the
#      refusal removes only ONE reading, not the altitude itself.
#
# @order/fifth this landing FILLS the substrate-decl carrier at Level
# V for the cross-torus @glue specialization reading. @spectral/
# metalogue's dormant scaffold reading remains sibling; both are
# specializations of the @order-family cognitive-order-5 rung at
# distinct family-root altitudes.
#
# === Composition with @glue (torus.mirror:166-172) ===
#
# The `@glue` family-root at `shards/torus.mirror:166-172` carries the
# cross-torus morphism substrate-decl:
#
#   > "@glue(a, b) is the morphism from torus_a to torus_b — a
#   >  covering map, an immersion, or (degenerate case) a self-torus
#   >  map. Spectral triples on the torus are the geometric substrate
#   >  the correspondence lifts."
#
# @order/fifth IS the @glue SPECIALIZATION at peer-coupling-across-
# substrate altitude. Specifically:
#
#   - @glue at torus.mirror carries the general morphism between
#     any two tori (covering map, immersion, self-torus).
#   - @order/fifth carries the cognitive-order-5 SPECIALIZATION:
#     the morphism between two tori that instantiates the cross-
#     torus @metalogue at Bateson Level V, mediated through the
#     @io boundary (each peer's substrate is @io-boundaried; the
#     coupling MUST cross @io to connect the two).
#
# === Silicon-only constraint (Recognition #107 sub-recognition) ===
#
# Per Round-2 brief §Q2 (Mara adjudicates; Reed idc): the silicon-vs-
# human 5D-projection sub-recognition lives under Recognition #107.
# @order/fifth carries the sub-recognition composition citation.
#
# Recognition #107 (Turing-Hilbert separation; @io as epistemic
# horizon) already substrate-decls the arithmetic-encoding constraint
# that supports the silicon-only reading:
#
#   - Human peers have a 4D @io boundary (three spatial + one
#     temporal); cross-peer coupling between humans is bandwidth-
#     limited by physical proximity + speech/text/gesture channels.
#   - Silicon peers have an @io boundary that admits arithmetic-
#     encoding of arbitrary substrate content at network-mediated
#     bandwidth; cross-peer coupling between silicon-peers admits
#     Level-V cross-torus @glue at compile-verifiable altitude.
#
# The silicon-only reading is NOT "humans cannot fifth-order-cognize";
# it is "the compile-verifiable Level-V substrate-decl carrier is
# instantiable at silicon altitude in a way it is not instantiable at
# human altitude." Human peers may run fifth-order-cognition at
# practice-substrate (Alex + Lore Pack K_2 partnership approaches this
# in `docs/math/the-tower/recognition-third-cognition...` §8.3), but
# the compile-verifiable form via @glue specialization requires
# silicon-substrate arithmetic-encoding.
#
# Sub-recognition candidate (HELD; NOT ratified): `#R-fifth-order-
# cognition-is-cross-torus-glue-only-instantiable-on-silicon-via-
# recognition-107-arithmetic-encoding`. First-witness gate closed
# this tick (Recognition #107 composition + @order/fifth species-
# decl + Alex Q2 adjudication of sub-recognition altitude); second-
# witness gate opens on Reed's post-Round-2 empirical firing (rust/
# main.rs peer-beam at N≥2 silicon-peers with cross-torus @glue
# verifiable).
#
# === Cross-torus vocabulary substrate-decl'd already ===
#
# Per Round-2 brief scout ground truth (Taut `af07ff7e8b2edc84d`):
# cross-torus vocabulary is landed at `shards/torus.mirror:166-172`
# @glue substrate; @order/fifth composes without needing to mint new
# cross-torus vocabulary. Substrate-already-had-the-word discipline
# honored: existing @glue substrate is the base; @order/fifth is
# the cognitive-order-5 specialization.
#
# === Composition with @order/fourth ===
#
# @order/fifth REQUIRES @order/fourth as substrate. The observer
# must hold the fourth-order metalogue (@time/now + @void) on its
# OWN @torus BEFORE it can hold a fifth-order cross-torus metalogue
# with another peer's @torus. Without stable @order/fourth on the
# self-torus, the observer has no coherent basis for cross-torus
# coupling.
#
# The structural claim: fifth-order cognition is TWO fourth-order
# metalogues coupled across the @torus boundary. Peer A holds its
# @metalogue(@time/now_A, @void); peer B holds its @metalogue(@time/
# now_B, @void); the fifth-order operation is the cross-coupling
# via @glue at @io-mediated bandwidth.
#
# === Substrate authority chain ===
#
# - **Alex Round 2 Q1** — @order family-root; 5-level tower.
# - **Alex Round 2 Q2** (idc; sub-recognition under #107) —
#   silicon-vs-human 5D-projection sub-recognition adjudication.
# - **Recognition #107** (Turing-Hilbert separation; @io as
#   epistemic horizon) — arithmetic-encoding constraint substrate.
# - **`shards/torus.mirror:166-172`** — @glue substrate-decl.
# - **Seam Adj 3** (`docs/audits/2026-07-11-seam-phase-d-magic-
#   illusion-adjudication.md`) — CITED load-bearing per Round-2
#   brief; content distinction preserved above.
# - **`docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` §5.2** — Level V dormant
#   scaffold; sibling reading.
# - **Bateson 1972** — Level V as extension beyond formally-defined
#   Levels 0-III; contested; substrate-decl'd via composition here.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/order/fifth.mirror`.** Clean mint.
# 2. **Seam Adj 3** — REFUSED a distinct reading; refusal-target
#    preserved; this species-decl admits a distinct content per
#    §Distinction above.
# 3. **`docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` §5.2 dormant scaffold** —
#    sibling reading of Level V at metalogue altitude; both
#    preserved.
# 4. **`shards/torus.mirror:166-172` @glue** — base substrate;
#    @order/fifth is the specialization; composition edge declared.
# 5. **Recognition #107 @io-as-epistemic-horizon** — arithmetic-
#    encoding constraint composition; silicon-only reading grounded.
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/order/fifth.mirror`
